mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course, as an important component of the long-term integrated teaching design for undergraduate, master's and doctoral studies in orthodontics, is dedicated to cultivating outstanding talents who integrate multiple disciplines, possess the ability to understand, doubt, think, believe and act, and are innovative, applied and compound.</p>
<p>Adopting a teaching model that combines online and offline learning, as well as case analysis, we center on learning to cultivate logical thinking, critical thinking, expression and presentation, and international communication skills for scientific issues in orthodontics and related disciplines (including basic, clinical, and related specialties), foster innovative thinking and behavioral habits, and establish a concept of serving the public in the field of big health.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
